m/2012/11/boises-proposed-thoughtcrime-ordinance.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-8813730938827482825' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/8813730938827482825' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-1682327196"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="November 16, 2012 at 12:35 PM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-151732237381079535</id><published>2012-11-16T09:47:39.433-07:00</published><updated>2012-11-16T09:47:39.433-07:00</updated><title type='text'>Will...excellent piece as usual.  I assume that th...</title><content type='html'>Will...excellent piece as usual.  I assume that there is still a significant LDS population in Boise; I&amp;#39;m also assuming that many of them own businesses.  I wonder how this latest edict will play out against a group whose sincerely held beliefs may incline them to violate said edict.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/8813730938827482825/comments/default/151732237381079535'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/8813730938827482825/comments/default/151732237381079535'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2012/11/boises-proposed-thoughtcrime-ordinance.html?showComment=1353084459433#c151732237381079535' title=''/><author><name>Captain Kirk</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/13986421255083663795</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2012/11/boises-proposed-thoughtcrime-ordinance.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-8813730938827482825' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/8813730938827482825' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-1078117220"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="November 16, 2012 at 9:47 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-8839031294665653137</id><published>2012-11-16T08:46:22.127-07:00</published><updated>2012-11-16T08:46:22.127-07:00</updated><title type='text'>Ever tried talking to the average Joe about privat...</title><content type='html'>Ever tried talking to the average Joe about private property rights?  What a disaster, as most people seem to think it is perfectly OK for some outside force (government) to dictate what others do with their own property.  &lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;I&amp;#39;m not sure we can turn things around until the majority of people in this country understand the role private property (and full control over that property) plays in a truly free society.  Until that happens, I think we&amp;#39;re screwed.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Great piece, as usual, Will.&lt;br /&gt;</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/8813730938827482825/comments/default/8839031294665653137'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/8813730938827482825/comments/default/8839031294665653137'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2012/11/boises-proposed-thoughtcrime-ordinance.html?showComment=1353080782127#c8839031294665653137' title=''/><author><name>Michael</name><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/blank.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2012/11/boises-proposed-thoughtcrime-ordinance.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-8813730938827482825' source='http://www.blogge